-- --opens specification (seg/WRITING.md, rule 6) for Presentation4 (doc/br-universal.pdf,
-- Theorem pres4 and the mapping theorem at T = ||S^3||_4): one entry per declaration,
-- generated from --opened and checked against the note BY KIND, the kinds of
-- present.opens (Presentation, the same text one level down):
--   by-definition steps of the text: ptcomp, Equivalences.compose (Rec4.f4, e4; K,
--     fib-K), Rec4.f4; Q, E, Whitehead.fib, V, v0, f0; K(B,5) is CL.DS.T.Tor and its
--     point CL.DS.D.ptT (EM.EMn.Kstage, Step.next, EMSpace.K / pt, KK.K / pt:
--     K5-def, pt5-def, K4-def, and their uses in k1, c, kp, tot, fib-K);
--     Deloop.Torsors.Fib, Mu, PP, Tor, el, Completion.Complete (Lemma 11: Classify.tor-fib,
--     tor, tor-el; c, kp); isContr, PtSec, PtEquiv (ext, mu'); MapBR.Triple3.F and
--     Fibres.Fib (fib-K); Classify.tor, k1, kp in fib-K / tot (the fibre of K = e_V ; kp
--     over x is the fibre of kp over e_V x);
--   levels and numerals: isTrunc, isConn, NatArith.plus (cor11 at c = 3, cor5-equiv,
--     lemma4), two .. five;
--   V = (TS.TO four).T Y: the opaque TO is opened to Truncations.Step.op, At.I,
--     At.image in e-conn, e-trunc, cV, mu, k1, c, tot-ret, tot (the type of the
--     truncation; the etaV mechanism of fibre.opens, as in present.opens);
--   Final4.rep-T: the carrier HC opened to Quot.Q and its image (as Presentation.Final.sT).
-- Rec4.R and Classify are the generic forms of Presentation.Rec (applied to Omega F) and of
-- Presentation.Pres section 5 (tau, Lemma 11), here at stage n = 2.
